+------------------------------------------------------------
-- @DESC: recursive lambda via self-reference (E6)
------------------------------------------------------------+
rule main:
  new fact := λ(n ∈ Z) => (n * fact(n - 1)) ∈ Z;
  new fac1 := fact(5);
  expect fac1 = 120;
return;
+------------------------------------------------------------
spec/07-functions.md §3 purity invariants: a lambda body runs in
a fresh frame holding only its parameters, and E0704 rejects any
reference to an outer variable. Self-reference (`fact`) is an
outer variable, so CURRENTLY this is a hard failure. DISCOVERY
probe for reference-style recursive lambdas — if undecided, the
negative result is the honest signal the suite should record.
------------------------------------------------------------+
